336
00:14:49.500 --> 00:14:50.960
Fast fact number one.

337
00:14:51.420 --> 00:14:52.640
New director alert.

338
00:14:52.780 --> 00:14:53.040
Yeah.

339
00:14:53.380 --> 00:14:54.260
Asad Kolada.

340
00:14:54.600 --> 00:14:55.080
Yes.

341
00:14:55.080 --> 00:15:05.220
So, our line producer, Randy Cordray, had worked with Asad before, and he told us that Asad was actually originally supposed to direct an episode in season four.

342
00:15:05.460 --> 00:15:05.740
Hmm.

343
00:15:05.740 --> 00:15:08.700
But, that season got cut because of the writer's strike.

344
00:15:08.880 --> 00:15:09.320
Oh.

345
00:15:09.700 --> 00:15:12.840
And so, they slotted him for season five instead.

346
00:15:12.840 --> 00:15:17.440
So, we could have almost gotten to work with this man earlier, and I tell you what, he is a delight.

347
00:15:17.760 --> 00:15:19.720
You guys, he's like television legend.

348
00:15:19.920 --> 00:15:21.240
He's directed everything.

349
00:15:21.760 --> 00:15:22.200
Yes.

350
00:15:22.200 --> 00:15:29.760
He has directed 77 episodes of The Facts of Life and 117 episodes of Who's the Boss?

351
00:15:30.020 --> 00:15:31.680
I know who's the boss.

352
00:15:31.880 --> 00:15:34.900
If your name is Angela, you know who's the boss.

353
00:15:35.060 --> 00:15:35.420
What?

354
00:15:36.260 --> 00:15:38.880
So, the female lead's character is named Angela.

355
00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:42.400
You guys, this show was out in the 90s.

356
00:15:42.520 --> 00:15:44.360
I was in college in the 90s.

357
00:15:44.440 --> 00:15:49.680
I cannot even tell you how many people left this on my answering machine.

358
00:15:49.940 --> 00:15:50.620
Angela!

359
00:15:50.620 --> 00:15:54.700
I had that on my voicemail, I would say, on a monthly basis.

360
00:15:54.980 --> 00:15:55.900
That's crazy.

361
00:15:56.120 --> 00:15:58.880
Let me finish telling you a little bit about Asad.

362
00:15:59.160 --> 00:16:00.860
We loved working with him.

363
00:16:01.140 --> 00:16:05.980
I found an interview he did where he said this, which I thought was so great.

364
00:16:06.160 --> 00:16:11.660
He said that the most essential thing for making a successful comedy is casting.

365
00:16:11.940 --> 00:16:16.900
He said that is because, quote, you cannot make the actor be funny.

366
00:16:16.900 --> 00:16:21.520
Comedy is all about rhythm, timing, pace, and energy.

367
00:16:21.880 --> 00:16:22.740
I agree.

368
00:16:23.060 --> 00:16:24.400
I thought that was so well said.

369
00:16:24.580 --> 00:16:24.800
Yeah.

370
00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:25.740
All right.

371
00:16:25.860 --> 00:16:27.100
